hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19221","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Ahmar ibn Jaziy, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: We used to take shelter toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because he kept his elbows away from his sides when prostrating."
